and dozens of distinguished speakers are  once again joining efforts to find best  solution for the transition towards a  more sustainable economy we were here  today from the policy makers here in the  heart of the European Union but also  from the EU Partners from across the  Atlantic and from all over the world  two years ago on the initiative of the  European commission president Ursula Von  delay and the European Union increased  its climate ambition they used 27 member  states endorsed ambitious climate  targets for 2030 and the objective to  reach climate neutrality by 2050. the  European green deal is the use growth  strategy with dedicated investment plan  to unlock Investments and finance for  the green transition in the European  Union and Beyond however since February  2022 the situation in Europe has  worsened dramatically War has returned  to all continent  Russia's invasion of Ukraine is not only  bringing unbearable suffering to the  Ukrainian people it is also threatening  the security and the sovereignty of the  EU and is causing hardship around the  world with the most vulnerable countries  affected the worst  for the European Union it is clear that  it is its dependency on Russia's fossil  energy Supply must come to an end  with the repower EU plan the European  commission proposes to to make the  eu-wide Energy System more resilient by  phasing out fossil fuels from Russia  well before 2030. diversify energy  supplies and boosting Energy Efficiency  as well as investment in renewable  energies while ensuring that secure and  clean energy remains affordable to  companies businesses and the households  the second edition of the EU sustainable  investment Summit is an opportunity to  send a clear signal that in spite of  Russia's attempt to disrupt the  international order the world needs to  remain United in its fight against  climate change and we are inviting all  of you to join us here today during the  day please use the tool called slider  where you can ask your questions and  make your comments let us know what you  think about some of the most important  issues these days in the European Union  but also in the world we're going to  hear from the speakers we're going to  hear from the panelists and the sessions  and we're going to hear the keynote  addresses and the first one to open this  year's event is coming from the  president of the European commission or  Solomon Tulane  distinguished guests colleagues  activists  investors and leaders across the field  of sustainability  I am delighted to open this year's  sustainable investment Summit  since we met last year  global economic growth forecasts may  have weakened  but our Collective commitment to  building a sustainable economy has  certainly not in fact  the business  security  and moral case  for the green transition has only become  stronger  the same fateful week Russia invaded  Ukraine in February  the leading Authority on climate change  the ipcc  issued a stark warning to the global  community  they demonstrated that the climate is  changing faster than our capacity to  adapt  and the message could not be clearer we  must speed up sustainable Investments  and increase their scope  now more than ever despite Russia's  attack to disrupt the international  order  the world must remain United in our  fight for peaceful fear and prosperous  future  I would like to focus on two points  today that you will cover in more depth  in the panels  first on public investment  which is needed to mobilize private  capital  and second on empowering workers with  skills to drive the green transition  so let's start with public investment  our immediate priority is tackling the  energy crisis which risks becoming an  economic and social crisis  already at last year's Summit  I spoke about the unsustainability of  the energy system  which is still dominated by fossil fuels  now since Russia's brutal attack on  Ukraine this has become even more  obvious  Putin is using fossil fuels as a weapon  against Europe  but Europe will not be blackmailed we  will not compromise on our values we are  determined to end our dependence on  Russian fossil fuels once and for all  and fast  for example by diversifying Supply  saving energy and accelerating the  rollout of Renewables let me give you  two figures  last year 41 of Europe's gas Imports  came from Russia  now today this figure is down to nine  percent pipeline gas  we were able to compensate these losses  through increased Supply by our trusted  Partners like the US and Norway  in parallel  we have filled our gas storages to over  92 percent  and this is significantly higher than it  was last year  and we have managed to save 15 of the  gas consumption  but we have to go and steer the medium  and long-term transition at the same  time so we have proposed re-power EU  an investment support to cut our  dependence on Russian fossil fuels by  accelerating the deployment of  Renewables  renewable energy is not only good for  the climate  it is also good for our independence  it is clean energy produced at home  gas pipelines are being built fit for  purpose for green hydrogen  interconnectors are being completed to  create a europe-wide electricity grid  to support the mass deployment of wind  and solar  so we are investing in the  infrastructure  and Technology  needed for full transition to a low  carbon economy  repower EU will come as additional  Firepower and acceleration on top of the  recovery and resilience plans of the EU  member states  to date the commission has given the  green light to nearly 500 billion euros  from Next Generation EU  of which half support the green  transition  this includes measures in sustainable  mobility in Energy Efficiency  investments in Renewables and in grids  let me give you some examples  and France's plan  85 000 ecological bonuses have already  been distributed  to support the uptake of clean vehicles  and this is just the start  because much of our public investment  is designed to help de-risk and mobilize  private capital  like for example in Italy's plan  where Next Generation EU funds are being  used to boost their National Innovation  fund  this is to finance private Investments  that have a positive impact on research  and Innovation for low-carbon economy  the measure in Italy aims to support 250  small and medium-sized Enterprises with  700 million euros in sustainable  investment so  this is the right way to go  because we need entrepreneurs and  private investment to help get the job  done  and that's why we are here today  the green Innovation is here  the public investment is here and the  path is clear  this is a truly exciting moment for all  of us who believe in sustainable  progress  and this brings me to my second point  people  the so-called human capital  this is a Core theme of today's Summit  and for very good reason  they are entrepreneurs with big projects  and dreams  and companies with ambitious plans to  decarbonize  who simply cannot find the professionals  with the green and digital skills to  work with them  in Europe right now we have the  strongest labor market in decades but at  the same time  we have a serious shortage of the right  skills  this is a trend that has picked up  especially in the last two years  as we recovered from the pandemic  lockdowns  The munich-based ifo Institute has found  a growing shortage of skilled workers in  almost every EU member state  across economic sectors  from manufacturing to services  for example in construction which is a  pivotal sector for the clean energy  transition  nearly 35 percent of EU firms  report impairments due to shortage of  skilled workers  that is why I have proposed to make 2023  the European year of skills to focus our  attention and sustainable investment on  this crucial issue  at European level we've set Targets on  re and upskilling and made available  large amounts of EU funding  nearly 1.5 billion euros in Next  Generation used so far  and 4.2 billion from the European social  fund  but it is about more than funding it is  about bringing Industry and Training  providers together  employers associations with trade unions  the goal is to better match Skilling  strategies with the economy's need in  our labor market  and this is an approach we are  pioneering with a pact for skills  we have created 12 large-scale  Partnerships offering Skilling  opportunities  to 6 million EU citizens of working age  for example nearly 1 500 graduates and  workers have already received training  in the offshore renewable energy sector  this is great news because offshore wind  for example in the Baltic Sea and the  North Sea is a huge and clean power  source  both for Europe's energy independence  from Russia and to meet our climate  ambitions  because it is the people and their  know-how who drive positive change  ladies and gentlemen  if we take a step back  we have identified where investment is  needed  in clean energy  in Green Tech and skills  and the list goes on for we haven't even  spoken about biodiversity  the potential of green Innovation and  growth is immense  but to unlock this potential we need to  shift the entire Financial system  away from an unsustainable practices  towards Investments that are truly  future proof  the European Union has created the most  advanced sustainable Finance framework  globally  we're working hard to walk the talk on  sustainable investment for example we're  on track to be the world's largest  issuer of green months to finance  Europe's climate-related reforms and  Investments  so far we have issued 28 billion euros  in green bonds  continuously attracting significant  oversubscription for our issuances  this is a boost not only to Europe's  transition  but to the green bond market itself as  investors will have access to a very  Liquid Green curve over time  sustainability is much more than the  right thing to do  it is although the safest  and the smartest investment we can make  betting on a low-carbon economy  that gives Back To Nature more than it  takes  and reinforces our security  is the most certain economic Trend in  the coming years and decades  thank you for your leadership  thank you for your pledges  and I wish you an exciting Summit  and following the words of the European  commission president on the importance  for the EU to work with the trusted  Partners we're going to hear next from  the prime minister of Canada Justin  Trudeau  hello everyone  bonjouratos it's great to be joining you  for the EU sustainable investment Summit
 

